            "label": "Architecture review call",
            "raw": "https://projects.a4842009-a9ac-4953-ae7b-f33baa0d53ed/evidence?item=ded7135b-16a1-480e-91af-fb7aa0a7f017#evidence-ded7135b-16a1-480e-91af-bb7aa0a7f017",
            "href": null,
            "targetId": null,
            "resolves": false
          }
        ],
        "answer": "We chose logical replication for the pilot cut-over based on a decision made on September 9, 2026. The decision involved two mechanisms: logical replication and an application-layer dual-write. After considering the implications, logical replication was chosen because the dual-write option would impact nineteen write paths in the payments service and require four to five weeks of work. Additionally, it was determined that rollback benefits were not necessary at the pilot volume, making logical replication the more efficient choice. This decision is documented in the architecture review call which explicitly rejected dual-write due to its complexity and workload requirements. \n\nFor more details, see the decision [Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication](https://projects.a4842009-a9ac-4953-ae7b-f33baa0d53ed/decisions?decision=82015c68-3f1b-416a-aee7-9ffad8f5c1fd) and the source from the [Architecture review call](https://projects.a4842009-a9ac-4953-ae7b-f33baa0d53ed/evidence?item=ded7135b-16a1-480e-91af-fb7aa0a7f017#evidence-ded7135b-16a1-480e-91af-bb7aa0a7f017).",
        "finishReason": "stop"
      },
